1
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,880
Here are the first 3 patterns of a tile design.

2
00:00:10,930 --> 00:00:12,620
Pattern 1 has 3 tiles.

3
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,370
Pattern 2 has 5 tiles.

4
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:16,660
Pattern 3 has 7 tiles.

5
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:19,140
How many tiles will Pattern 4 have?

6
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:22,800
Pause the video and work it out.

7
00:00:22,850 --> 00:00:26,560
Each new pattern has 1 more tile on each arm of the L.

8
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:29,260
That is 2 more tiles each time.

9
00:00:29,310 --> 00:00:30,540
7 plus 2 is 9.

10
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:33,090
Pattern 4 has 9 tiles.

11
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:40,170
Remember: a quick way to see an add or subtract rule is to write the differences between the terms.

12
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:41,540
7, 11, 15, 19.

13
00:00:41,590 --> 00:00:46,290
The differences are plus 4, plus 4, plus 4.

14
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:48,460
Look at these 2 sequences.

15
00:00:48,510 --> 00:00:49,550
4, 7, 10, 13.

16
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:50,890
And 1, 4, 9, 16.

17
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:54,900
Which one goes up by the same amount every time?

18
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:58,550
Pause the video and decide.

19
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:02,100
4, 7, 10, 13 goes up by 3 every time.

20
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:06,970
But 1, 4, 9, 16 goes up by 3, then 5, then 7.

21
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:13,850
A sequence is linear when the differences between terms next to each other are all the same.

22
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,700
A linear sequence can go up, or it can go down.

23
00:01:17,750 --> 00:01:22,930
30, 26, 22, 18 is linear, with differences of negative 4.

24
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:25,190
Look at the tile pattern again.

25
00:01:25,240 --> 00:01:29,390
Every pattern has 1 corner tile, and 2 equal arms.

26
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:32,400
In Pattern 3, each arm has 3 tiles.

27
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:34,770
1 plus 3 plus 3 is 7.

28
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:37,960
So you can jump straight to any pattern.

29
00:01:38,010 --> 00:01:42,430
Pattern 6 has 1 plus 6 plus 6, which is 13 tiles.

30
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:43,150
Your turn.

31
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,450
How many tiles are in Pattern 8?

32
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,800
Pause the video and try it.

33
00:01:48,850 --> 00:01:52,830
Pattern 8 has 1 corner, and 2 arms of 8 tiles.

34
00:01:52,880 --> 00:01:55,840
1 plus 8 plus 8 is 17 tiles.

35
00:01:55,890 --> 00:02:00,020
Square numbers come from square patterns: 1, 4, 9, 16.

36
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:02,190
The differences are 3, 5, 7.

37
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:06,610
They are not equal, so the sequence is not linear.

38
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:11,470
Triangular numbers come from triangle patterns: 1, 3, 6, 10.

39
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,730
The differences are 2, 3, 4.

40
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:17,110
This sequence is not linear either.

41
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:18,440
Here is the method.

42
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:24,920
Step 1: write the difference between every pair of terms that are next to each other.

43
00:02:24,970 --> 00:02:30,060
Step 2: if all the differences are equal, the sequence is linear.

44
00:02:30,110 --> 00:02:34,900
Step 3: if even one difference is different, it is not linear.

45
00:02:34,950 --> 00:02:40,550
Step 4: to continue a linear sequence, keep adding the same difference.

46
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,910
Is this sequence linear?

47
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:44,740
3, 6, 11, 18.

48
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:47,010
The differences are 3, 5 and 7.

49
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:50,790
They are not all equal, so it is not linear.

50
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:54,550
What about 52, 45, 38, 31?

51
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:57,060
The differences are all negative 7.

52
00:02:57,110 --> 00:02:59,540
So this sequence is linear.

53
00:02:59,590 --> 00:03:02,720
Pattern 1 is a square made of 4 matchsticks.

54
00:03:02,770 --> 00:03:07,820
Each new pattern adds 1 more square to the row, sharing a side.

55
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:11,520
A new square needs only 3 new matchsticks.

56
00:03:11,570 --> 00:03:14,680
So the sequence is 4, 7, 10, 13, 16.

57
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:17,790
Pattern 5 has 16 matchsticks.

58
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,870
Which pattern uses 31 matchsticks?

59
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:25,300
31 minus 4 is 27, and 27 divided by 3 is 9 steps.

60
00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:29,300
9 steps after Pattern 1 is Pattern 10.

61
00:03:29,350 --> 00:03:34,560
In the L-shaped design, is there a pattern with exactly 50 tiles?

62
00:03:34,610 --> 00:03:37,810
Every pattern is 1 corner plus 2 equal arms.

63
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:43,170
2 equal arms make an even number, and 1 more makes an odd number.

64
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:45,810
Every term is odd, but 50 is even.

65
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:49,080
So no pattern has exactly 50 tiles.

66
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:51,920
Is 1, 2, 4, 7, 11 a linear sequence?

67
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:53,650
Here is Kai's working.

68
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:56,410
Which line goes wrong first?

69
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:57,600
Line 2 is wrong.

70
00:03:57,650 --> 00:04:02,350
For a linear sequence, the differences themselves must be equal.

71
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:06,620
Here they are 1, 2, 3, 4, which are all different.

72
00:04:06,670 --> 00:04:09,220
So the sequence is not linear.

73
00:04:09,270 --> 00:04:15,000
In ten-pin bowling, the pins stand in a triangle: 1, then 2, then 3, then 4.

74
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:18,210
That makes 10, a triangular number.

75
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:21,240
A chessboard has 8 rows of 8 squares.

76
00:04:21,290 --> 00:04:24,500
8 times 8 is 64, a square number.

77
00:04:24,550 --> 00:04:30,450
And the seats in a cinema row are numbered 1, 2, 3, 4: a linear sequence.

78
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,780
One last question.

79
00:04:31,830 --> 00:04:36,040
Pattern 1 uses 5 matchsticks, and each new pattern adds 4.

80
00:04:36,090 --> 00:04:38,840
How many matchsticks are in Pattern 7?

81
00:04:38,890 --> 00:04:42,590
Pause the video and work it out.

82
00:04:42,640 --> 00:04:46,200
From Pattern 1 to Pattern 7 is 6 steps.

83
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:51,290
6 times 4 is 24, and 5 plus 24 is 29 matchsticks.

84
00:04:51,340 --> 00:04:55,720
To remember: count the pieces in each pattern to make a sequence.

85
00:04:55,770 --> 00:04:59,070
The picture shows you why the rule works.

86
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:02,540
A sequence is linear if all the differences are equal.

87
00:05:02,590 --> 00:05:04,440
It can go up or down.

88
00:05:04,490 --> 00:05:08,660
Square numbers and triangular numbers are not linear.

89
00:05:08,710 --> 00:05:13,270
To reach a later pattern, count the steps, not the patterns.

90
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:18,430
Great work! Now practise lesson 9.2 on Camday.
